cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Untyped threat modeling"
abstract: >-
  Automated threat modeling maps parsed entities onto a taxonomy of component
  types before analysing them. That mapping step is the index the rule set is
  keyed against, and it bounds what the method can find: a component the
  taxonomy cannot name is a component the rules cannot reach, and the omission
  is not visible in the output. This work describes and implements the same job
  done without the mapping step. A node is an integer and an unordered bag of
  raw strings exactly as they appeared in the source; an edge is a pair of
  integers. Interpretation is performed by a model reading the strings rather
  than by code matching them, so the method degrades to inference at the
  boundary of its knowledge rather than to silence. Includes an audit mode that
  enumerates every vertex against published threat categories, which is
  possible because threat categories are closed and published while component
  types are neither.
authors:
  - family-names: Barkai
    given-names: Jacob
type: software
